# LAB 3 - Deployment

## Goal

Created a Deployment and understood rolling updates and rollbacks.

## Commands Used

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

kubectl get deployments

kubectl get rs

kubectl get pods

kubectl describe deployment nginx-deployment

kubectl set image deployment/nginx-deployment nginx-container=nginx:1.29

kubectl rollout history deployment/nginx-deployment

kubectl rollout undo deployment/nginx-deployment

## What I Learned

- Deployment manages ReplicaSets.

- ReplicaSet manages Pods.

- Deployment creates a new ReplicaSet during updates.

- Rolling updates avoid downtime.

- Rollbacks reuse older ReplicaSets.

- Old ReplicaSets are preserved for rollback.

## Production Scenario

Deployment allows zero-downtime upgrades and safe rollbacks in production environments.
